          "name": "Wallbreaker (Poison)",
          "pokemon": "Nidoking",
          "shiny": false,
          "gender": "M",
          "levels": [],
          "description": "<p>Nidoking finds a solid place on Poison teams as the premier special attacker thanks to Sheer Force and its solid movepool giving it a unique role of helping with the Steel matchup. Earth Power demolishes the Steel- and Poison-types that can easily come in on its teammates such as <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/heatran/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Heatran</a>, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/gholdengo/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Gholdengo</a>, and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/toxapex/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Toxapex</a>. Flamethrower deals with Steel-types not threatened by Earth Power such as <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/corviknight/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Corviknight</a>, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/ferrothorn/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Ferrothorn</a>, and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/scizor/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Scizor</a>. Ice Beam removes problematic Ground- and Flying-types like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/hippowdon/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Hippowdon</a>, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/gliscor/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Gliscor</a>, and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/zapdos/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Zapdos</a>. Stealth Rock can help chip foes that can swap into Earth Power like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/charizard-mega-y/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Mega Charizard Y</a>. Alternatively, Thunderbolt can be run to complete the BoltBeam coverage and hit Water-types like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/pelipper/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Pelipper</a>, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/dondozo/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Dondozo</a>, and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/mantine/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Mantine</a>, which otherwise wall Nidoking. Choice Scarf <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/sneasler/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Sneasler</a> forms a solid offensive core with Nidoking. Sneasler not only removes specially defensive targets like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/goodra-hisui/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Hisuian Goodra</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/blissey/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Blissey</a>, but also removes faster targets like Mega Charizard Y and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/volcarona/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Volcarona</a> if running Rock Slide, while Nidoking deals with threats that would stop Sneasler like Gholdengo and Toxapex. <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/venusaur-mega/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Mega Venusaur</a> handles the Water- and Ground-type foes that would overwhelm Nidoking such as <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/barraskewda/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Barraskewda</a>, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/gyarados-mega/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Mega Gyarados</a>, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/swampert/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Swampert</a>, and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/mamoswine/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Mamoswine</a>. <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/muk-alola/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Alolan Muk</a> deals with Ghost- and Psychic-types such as <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/zoroark-hisui/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Hisuian Zoroark</a>, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/raichu-alola/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Alolan Raichu</a>, and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/tapu-lele/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Tapu Lele</a>, which pose a significant issue for Nidoking. <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/slowking-galar/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Galarian Slowking</a> can take on threats such as Choice Specs <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/latios/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Latios</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/tornadus-therian/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Tornadus-T</a> and use Future Sight to help overwhelm special walls like Swampert. <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/crobat/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Crobat</a> is immune to Ground-type moves from Pokemon like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/great-tusk/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Great Tusk</a>, can use Defog to remove entry hazards to provide safe entry for Nidoking, and can deal with threats like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/gallade-mega/national-dex-monotype/\" hreflang=\"en\">Mega Gallade</a>.</p>",
